      {
        "id": "AC-1",
        "text": "Under the default policy, `TRACE /x` and `CONNECT /x` yield unsupported method whether or not any route matches `/x`. [D-067]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 1364
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-2",
        "text": "With only `TRACE` enabled, a registered `TRACE /x` route is matched, `TRACE /y` with no matching pattern yields no match, `TRACE` on a path with only a `GET` route yields method mismatch, and `CONNECT /x` still yields unsupported method. [wave decision: TRACE/CONNECT policy]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 1365
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-3",
        "text": "With `CONNECT` enabled, `CONNECT` behaves as `TRACE` does in the previous criterion, and in neither case does a registration under `Method.any()` serve the enabled method. [wave decision: TRACE/CONNECT policy; D-036]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 1366
      }
    ],
