    "requirement": "The system shall disable `TRACE` and `CONNECT` routing by default, so that both yield the unsupported-method result whatever the path, and shall provide a router policy that enables each of them separately, after which an enabled method routes like any other method and is registered only by naming it.",
    "rationale": "Covers D-067, D-070 and the wave decision on the TRACE/CONNECT policy. On the TinyHttpd adapter the policy also governs a `CONNECT` with an origin-form or absolute-form target; authority-form `CONNECT` is answered `501` by TinyHttpd before dispatch (deferred TinyHttpd gap under D-020, wave 3).",
